<span class="label">Treatment Journey</span><h2 class="title">Your Full Mouth Implant <em>Procedure</em></h2><p class="desc">From consultation to final prosthesis — the entire journey typically requires two visits to Istanbul over 5–6 months.</p></div><div class="proc-timeline " data-anim="up"><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">1</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Pre-Arrival</span><h3>Digital Planning</h3><p>Before you travel, VeaHealth coordinates a full diagnostic workup — panoramic X-rays, 3D CBCT scan, and digital treatment planning. Your surgeon designs implant placement virtually to ensure optimal positioning.</p><ul><li>Medical history &#038; consultation via video</li><li>Digital X-rays &#038; CBCT scan uploaded</li><li>3D surgical guide designed</li><li>Final treatment plan &#038; quote confirmed</li><li>Travel &#038; accommodation arranged</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">2</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Day 1–2 — Istanbul</span><h3>Surgery &#038; Temporary Teeth</h3><p>Under IV sedation or general anesthesia, 4–6 implants are placed per arch. Any failing teeth are extracted. Temporary acrylic teeth are attached the same day — you walk out with a full smile.</p><ul><li>IV sedation or general anesthesia</li><li>Tooth extractions (if needed)</li><li>4–6 implants placed per arch</li><li>Immediate temporary prosthesis attached</li><li>Post-op instructions &#038; medications</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">3</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Day 3–7 — Istanbul</span><h3>Healing &#038; Adjustments</h3><p>You remain in Istanbul for 5–7 days for daily check-ups. Swelling peaks at 48 hours. Your surgeon adjusts the temporary teeth for comfort and verifies healing is on track before you return home.</p><ul><li>Daily wound inspection</li><li>Suture removal (day 7–10)</li><li>Temporary teeth bite adjustment</li><li>Pain management monitored</li><li>Soft diet guidance provided</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">4</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Month 1–4</span><h3>Osseointegration</h3><p>Implants fuse with your jawbone over 3–6 months. You wear temporary teeth during this period and follow a gradual diet progression. VeaHealth monitors your healing remotely via photos and video calls.</p><ul><li>Bone integration occurs naturally</li><li>Temporary teeth remain in place</li><li>Gradual return to normal diet</li><li>Remote check-ins every 2 weeks</li><li>No travel required during healing</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">5</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Month 4–6 — Return Visit</span><h3>Final Prosthesis Placement</h3><p>You return to Istanbul for 3–5 days. The temporary bridge is removed and digital impressions are taken. Your final zirconia prosthesis is fabricated, tested, and permanently attached.</p><ul><li>Temporary prosthesis removed</li><li>Digital impressions &#038; bite registration</li><li>Final zirconia bridge crafted (2–3 days)</li><li>Try-in with shade and bite verification</li><li>Permanent attachment &#038; warranty docs</li></ul></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cost" id="pricing" data-surface="dark"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Transparent Pricing</span><h2 class="title title-white">What You&#8217;ll Pay — <em>Guaranteed</em></h2><p class="desc desc-white">VeaHealth locks in your price before travel. All costs include surgery, implants, temporary teeth, final prosthesis, and lifetime warranty on fixtures.</p></div><div class="cost-cards " data-anim="up"><div class="cost-card"><h3>UK / US</h3><div class="location">London, New York</div><div class="cost-price">£15,000+</div><div class="cost-note">per arch</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>All-on-4 procedure</li><li>Standard implant brands</li><li>Temporary acrylic teeth</li><li>Final zirconia bridge</li><li>5-year warranty</li><li>No travel support</li></ul></div><div class="cost-card featured">
<span class="cost-tag">Best Value</span><h3>VeaHealth Istanbul</h3><div class="location">Istanbul, Turkey</div><div class="cost-price">£4,500</div><div class="cost-note">all-inclusive per arch</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>All-on-4 or All-on-6 technique</li><li>Straumann or Nobel Biocare implants</li><li>3D-guided surgery</li><li>Same-day temporary prosthesis</li><li>Premium zirconia final bridge</li><li>Lifetime warranty on implants</li><li>3-year warranty on prosthesis</li><li>Airport VIP transfers</li><li>7 nights hotel coordination</li><li>24/7 VeaHealth concierge</li></ul></div><div class="cost-card"><h3>Europe</h3><div class="location">Germany, Spain</div><div class="cost-price">€9,000+</div><div class="cost-note">per arch</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>All-on-4 standard protocol</li><li>Mid-range implants</li><li>Temporary teeth</li><li>Acrylic or hybrid bridge</li><li>2-year warranty</li><li>Limited travel assistance</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="recovery" id="recovery"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Post-Treatment</span><h2 class="title">Recovery &#038; <em>Aftercare</em></h2><p class="desc">Full mouth implant recovery is gradual but predictable. Most patients resume normal activities within 7–10 days and full chewing function within 3–6 months.</p></div><div class="rec-timeline " data-anim="up"><div class="rec-phase"><div class="rec-phase-num">1</div>
<span class="rec-phase-tag">Day 1–7</span><h3>Immediate Post-Op</h3><ul><li>Swelling peaks at 48 hours</li><li>Bruising may appear (normal)</li><li>Soft/liquid diet only</li><li>Pain managed with medication</li><li>Daily clinic check-ups</li></ul></div><div class="rec-phase"><div class="rec-phase-num">2</div>
<span class="rec-phase-tag">Week 2–4</span><h4>Early Healing</h4><ul><li>Swelling subsides completely</li><li>Sutures dissolve or removed</li><li>Gradual return to soft solids</li><li>No hard/chewy foods yet</li><li>Remote VeaHealth check-ins</li></ul></div><div class="rec-phase"><div class="rec-phase-num">3</div>
<span class="rec-phase-tag">Month 2–3</span><h4>Osseointegration</h4><ul><li>Bone fusion progressing</li><li>Normal diet resuming gradually</li><li>Temporary teeth feel stable</li><li>Oral hygiene routine established</li><li>Monthly photo updates to clinic</li></ul></div><div class="rec-phase"><div class="rec-phase-num">4</div>
<span class="rec-phase-tag">Month 4–6</span><h4>Final Restoration</h4><ul><li>Full osseointegration complete</li><li>Return to Istanbul for final bridge</li><li>Permanent prosthesis placed</li><li>Full chewing function restored</li><li>Biannual check-ups begin</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="evidence" id="evidence" data-surface="dark"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Clinical Evidence</span><h2 class="title title-white">What the <em>Studies Show</em></h2></div><div class="ev-grid " data-anim="up"><div class="ev-card"><div class="ev-num">95–98%</div><p class="ev-lbl">Implant survival rate for All-on-4/6 at 10 years across multiple systematic reviews — matching or exceeding individual implant protocols with significantly faster treatment times.</p><div class="ev-src">Maló et al. (2016) · Clinical Implant Dentistry</div></div><div class="ev-card"><div class="ev-num">3.2%</div><p class="ev-lbl">Prosthetic complication rate (crown fracture, screw loosening) over 10 years — manageable issues that are easily repaired without compromising the underlying implants.</p><div class="ev-src">Pjetursson et al. (2018) · Systematic review</div></div><div class="ev-card"><div class="ev-num">20+ yrs</div><p class="ev-lbl">Documented implant lifespan in well-maintained All-on-4 cases — confirming that with proper hygiene and regular professional care, full arch implants are truly a lifetime investment.</p><div class="ev-src">Journal of Oral Implantology · Long-term follow-up studies</div></div></div></div></section><section class="faq" id="faq"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Patient Questions</span><h2 class="title">Frequently Asked <em>Questions</em></h2></div><div class="faq-grid " data-anim="up"><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is full mouth implant surgery painful?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The procedure is performed under IV sedation or general anesthesia — you feel nothing during surgery. Post-op discomfort (swelling, soreness) peaks at 48 hours and is managed with prescribed pain medication and cold compresses. Most patients describe it as less painful than a single tooth extraction.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How long do full mouth dental implants last?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The titanium implants can last a lifetime with proper care — studies confirm 95%+ survival at 10 years and 20+ year longevity is common. The zirconia prosthesis may need replacement after 15–20 years due to wear. Biannual professional cleanings are essential for long-term success.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can I eat normally with full arch implants?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. After the initial healing period (3–6 months), you can eat all foods without restriction — including steak, nuts, apples, and corn on the cob. Chewing power is restored to 90–95% of natural teeth. No more dietary limitations like with dentures.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What if I don&#8217;t have enough bone?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The All-on-4/6 technique is specifically designed for patients with bone loss. Angled posterior implants avoid areas of deficiency and maximize contact with available bone. In 90% of cases, no bone grafting is needed. If grafting is required, VeaHealth identifies this during pre-treatment planning.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How many trips to Istanbul are required?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Two visits: the first for surgery and temporary teeth (7 days), and a second visit 4–6 months later for the final prosthesis (3–5 days). The healing phase in between is managed remotely by VeaHealth with no travel required.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is the warranty valid internationally?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. VeaHealth&#8217;s lifetime warranty on implants and 3-year warranty on prosthetics are valid worldwide. If a warranty issue arises after you return home, VeaHealth coordinates resolution remotely or via a local affiliated clinic in your country.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What implant brand will be used?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>VeaHealth exclusively uses Straumann and Nobel Biocare implants — the two most researched and validated brands globally. The specific brand, model, and serial numbers are documented in your treatment file and provided at completion. This is a contractual guarantee.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can smokers receive full mouth implants?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Smokers can receive implants, but tobacco significantly reduces success rates by impairing healing and osseointegration. VeaHealth strongly recommends stopping smoking at least 4–6 weeks before and 3–6 months after surgery. Compliance with smoking cessation measurably improves outcomes.</p></div></details></div></div></section><section class="cta-final" id="contact" data-surface="dark"><div class="cta-final-inner"><h2>Ready for Your<br>Complete Smile Transformation?</h2><p>VeaHealth coordinates your entire full mouth implant journey in Istanbul — premium brands, verified surgeons, and complete support from consultation to final restoration.</p><div class="cta-trust-row"><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Free Online Assessment</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Straumann &#038; Nobel Biocare Guaranteed</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> VIP Istanbul Concierge</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Lifetime Implant Warranty</div></div>
