<span class="label">Post-Op Care</span><h2 class="title">Recovery &#038; <em>Aftercare</em></h2><p class="desc">Healing is faster than most patients expect. VeaHealth supports you every step of the way — including after you fly home.</p></div><div class="care-grid " data-anim="up"><div class="care-card">
<span class="care-emoji">🧊</span><h3>Days 1–3</h3><p>Mild swelling and tenderness managed with prescribed medication and cold compresses. Most patients resume daily activities within 2–3 days of surgery.</p></div><div class="care-card">
<span class="care-emoji">🥣</span><h4>Diet Protocol</h4><p>Soft diet for the first 6–8 weeks (soups, mashed vegetables, yoghurt, smoothies). Semi-solids introduced gradually. Full diet resumes after final prosthesis is placed.</p></div><div class="care-card">
<span class="care-emoji">🪥</span><h4>Oral Hygiene</h4><p>Interdental brushes, superfloss, and water irrigators replace traditional flossing. Clean beneath the bridge daily to prevent peri-implantitis and protect long-term outcomes.</p></div><div class="care-card">
<span class="care-emoji">📱</span><h4>Remote Follow-Up</h4><p>VeaHealth provides digital check-ins after your return home. Photo assessments, direct coordinator access, and scheduled in-clinic review visits keep your treatment on track.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="evidence" id="evidence" data-surface="dark"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Clinical Evidence</span><h2 class="title title-white">What the <em>Studies Show</em></h2></div><div class="ev-grid " data-anim="up"><div class="ev-card"><div class="ev-num">93%+</div><p class="ev-lbl">Implant survival rate over 10 to 18 years of continuous clinical follow-up — confirming All-on-4 as a long-term solution.</p><div class="ev-src">Maló et al., 2019 · Longitudinal study 10–18 years</div></div><div class="ev-card"><div class="ev-num">~99%</div><p class="ev-lbl">Prosthesis survival rate over the same period — the full-arch bridge remained stable and functional in nearly all cases studied.</p><div class="ev-src">Maló et al., 2019 · Longitudinal study 10–18 years</div></div><div class="ev-card"><div class="ev-num">95%+</div><p class="ev-lbl">Single implant survival over 10 years — both approaches deliver comparable long-term results within their respective clinical indications.</p><div class="ev-src">Systematic review · Conventional implant protocols</div></div></div></div></section><section class="faq" id="faq"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Patient Questions</span><h2 class="title">Frequently Asked <em>Questions</em></h2></div><div class="faq-grid " data-anim="up"><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>Is All-on-4 painful?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">The procedure is performed under local anesthesia or sedation — no pain during surgery. Post-op discomfort (mild swelling, pressure) is managed with prescribed medication and typically resolves within a week. Most patients report less discomfort than anticipated.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>How long do All-on-4 implants last?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">The titanium implants themselves typically last 15–20+ years with proper care. The zirconia prosthesis is highly durable and may last the same timeframe, while acrylic bridges may require replacement after 10–12 years. Clinical studies confirm >93% implant survival at 18 years.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>Can smokers receive All-on-4 implants?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">Smokers are not excluded but tobacco significantly increases failure risk — nicotine reduces gingival blood flow and slows osseointegration. VeaHealth strongly advises reducing or stopping smoking at least 4–6 weeks before and after surgery to protect outcomes.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>What if one implant fails?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">A single failure rarely destabilizes the full arch — the remaining 3 implants maintain function. The failed fixture is removed, and options include bone grafting with replacement or switching to an All-on-6 configuration for added redundancy. Early detection through regular follow-ups is key.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>Are Turkish implant warranties valid internationally?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. VeaHealth&#8217;s warranties cover implant fixtures and prosthetic components and are honored internationally. Documentation is provided at treatment completion, and the warranty remains valid even after you return to your home country — with remote coordination available.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>Can people with bruxism get All-on-4?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">Yes, with precautions. Night guards and reinforced prosthetic materials are used to protect against excessive wear from grinding. VeaHealth evaluates bite forces during planning and designs the restoration to manage bruxism loads effectively.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
<span>How soon can I eat after the procedure?</span><div class="faq-arrow">+</div></div><div class="faq-a">You receive a fixed provisional bridge the same day, so you are never without teeth. A soft diet is maintained for 6–8 weeks. Once osseointegration is confirmed and the final bridge placed, you resume a full, unrestricted diet.</div></div><div class="faq-item" onclick="toggleFaq(this)"><div class="faq-q">
