<span class="label">Two Techniques</span><h2 class="title">Lateral vs <em>Crestal</em> Sinus Lift</h2><p class="desc">The approach depends on the amount of existing bone. VeaHealth&#8217;s surgeons select the optimal technique based on your 3D CBCT scan.</p></div><div class="types-grid " data-anim="up"><div class="type-card">
<span class="type-badge">Standard Technique</span><h3>Lateral Window Sinus Lift</h3><p>The gold standard for severe bone loss. A window is created in the lateral sinus wall, membrane lifted, and graft placed. Ideal when &lt;4mm of bone remains.</p><ul class="type-list"><li><strong>Indication:</strong> 1–5mm of existing bone height</li><li><strong>Technique:</strong> Lateral wall window + direct membrane access</li><li><strong>Graft volume:</strong> 2–4cc bone graft material per side</li><li><strong>Healing time:</strong> 6–9 months before implant placement</li><li><strong>Success rate:</strong> &gt;95% when executed by specialist</li><li><strong>Simultaneous implants:</strong> Possible if ≥5mm bone present</li></ul></div><div class="type-card">
<span class="type-badge">Less Invasive</span><h3>Crestal Sinus Lift</h3><p>A minimally invasive approach through the implant osteotomy site. Suitable when 5–7mm of bone exists — membrane lifted with osteotomes, implant placed simultaneously.</p><ul class="type-list"><li><strong>Indication:</strong> 5–8mm of existing bone height</li><li><strong>Technique:</strong> Internal approach via implant site</li><li><strong>Graft volume:</strong> 0.5–1cc bone graft per implant</li><li><strong>Healing time:</strong> 4–6 months (implant placed same day)</li><li><strong>Success rate:</strong> 92–95% in properly selected cases</li><li><strong>Advantage:</strong> No lateral window — faster recovery</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="procedure" id="procedure"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Treatment Journey</span><h2 class="title">Your Sinus Lift <em>Procedure</em></h2><p class="desc">From 3D planning to bone graft maturation and implant placement — typically 6–9 months total timeline.</p></div><div class="proc-timeline " data-anim="up"><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">1</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Pre-Arrival</span><h3>CBCT 3D Planning</h3><p>VeaHealth coordinates a comprehensive CBCT cone beam scan to measure bone height, sinus anatomy, and membrane thickness. Your surgeon designs the optimal lateral window position and graft volume virtually.</p><ul><li>3D sinus floor mapping</li><li>Bone height measurement at implant sites</li><li>Schneiderian membrane evaluation</li><li>Lateral vs crestal approach decided</li><li>Travel &#038; accommodation arranged</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">2</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Day 1 — Istanbul</span><h3>Sinus Lift Surgery</h3><p>Under local anesthesia or IV sedation, the lateral window is created using piezoelectric instruments. The Schneiderian membrane is gently elevated. Bone graft material fills the space beneath the membrane. A resorbable collagen membrane seals the window.</p><ul><li>Local anesthesia or IV sedation</li><li>Lateral window created (10×15mm)</li><li>Membrane lifted without perforation</li><li>Xenograft/allograft/synthetic bone packed</li><li>Collagen membrane placed</li><li>Wound sutured — post-op meds provided</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">3</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Month 1–6</span><h3>Bone Graft Maturation</h3><p>The graft consolidates over 4–9 months. Xenograft particles act as a scaffold for your natural bone to grow into. VeaHealth monitors healing remotely with CBCT scans at 3 and 6 months to confirm graft integration.</p><ul><li>Soft foods for 2 weeks</li><li>No nose-blowing for 4 weeks (critical)</li><li>Remote check-ins every 2 weeks</li><li>CBCT at month 3 &#038; 6 to assess bone quality</li><li>Graft fully matures by month 6–9</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">4</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Month 6–9 — Return Visit</span><h3>Implant Placement</h3><p>Once CBCT confirms the graft has consolidated into mature bone, you return to Istanbul for dental implant placement. The implants engage both the graft and native bone for optimal stability.</p><ul><li>Final CBCT confirms bone density</li><li>Implants placed into grafted bone</li><li>Standard osseointegration (3–4 months)</li><li>Crown/bridge fitted after integration</li><li>Lifetime warranty on implants</li></ul></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cost" id="pricing" data-surface="dark"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Transparent Pricing</span><h2 class="title title-white">What You&#8217;ll Pay — <em>Guaranteed</em></h2><p class="desc desc-white">VeaHealth locks in your price before travel. All costs include CBCT, surgery, bone graft, collagen membrane, and post-op monitoring.</p></div><div class="cost-cards " data-anim="up"><div class="cost-card"><h3>UK / US</h3><div class="location">London, New York</div><div class="cost-price">£2,800+</div><div class="cost-note">per sinus lift side</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>Lateral window technique</li><li>Standard bone graft</li><li>CBCT scan</li><li>Post-op follow-up (1–2 visits)</li><li>6-month monitoring</li></ul></div><div class="cost-card featured">
<span class="cost-tag">Best Value</span><h3>VeaHealth Istanbul</h3><div class="location">Istanbul, Turkey</div><div class="cost-price">£850</div><div class="cost-note">all-inclusive per side</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>3D-guided lateral window technique</li><li>Premium xenograft/allograft bone</li><li>Resorbable collagen membrane</li><li>CBCT scan pre &#038; post-op</li><li>Specialist oral surgeon</li><li>6-month remote monitoring</li><li>Post-op medication included</li><li>Airport VIP transfer</li><li>Hotel support coordination</li><li>24/7 VeaHealth concierge</li></ul></div><div class="cost-card"><h3>Europe</h3><div class="location">Germany, Spain</div><div class="cost-price">€1,800+</div><div class="cost-note">per sinus lift side</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>Standard lateral technique</li><li>Mid-range bone graft</li><li>CBCT scan</li><li>Follow-up appointments</li><li>3–6 month monitoring</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="faq" id="faq"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Patient Questions</span><h2 class="title">Frequently Asked <em>Questions</em></h2></div><div class="faq-grid " data-anim="up"><details class="faq-item"><summary>What is a sinus lift and when is it needed?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>A sinus lift (maxillary sinus augmentation) is a surgical procedure that adds bone to the upper jaw beneath the sinus cavity. It&#8217;s needed when there is insufficient bone height to place dental implants in the posterior upper jaw — typically after tooth loss causes bone resorption and sinus floor descent.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How long does a sinus lift take to heal?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Bone graft maturation takes 4–9 months depending on graft material and volume. Lateral window sinus lifts typically require 6–9 months before implant placement. Crestal sinus lifts heal faster (4–6 months) because implants are placed simultaneously with less graft volume.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is sinus lift surgery painful?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The procedure itself is performed under local anesthesia or IV sedation — you won&#8217;t feel pain during surgery. Post-operative discomfort is typically mild to moderate, managed with prescribed pain medication. Swelling peaks at 48–72 hours and resolves within a week. Most patients return to work within 3–5 days.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What is the success rate of sinus lift surgery?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Sinus lift surgery has a &gt;95% success rate when performed by experienced oral surgeons. Implants placed in grafted sinus bone achieve 95–98% survival at 10 years — statistically identical to implants in native bone. The most critical factor is allowing adequate healing time before implant loading.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can implants be placed at the same time as the sinus lift?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Yes, if ≥5mm of existing bone remains. This is called simultaneous placement. The implant is placed into the residual bone, and the sinus lift adds height around it. If &lt;4mm bone exists, a staged approach is recommended: sinus lift first, implants 6–9 months later once the graft has consolidated.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What bone graft materials does VeaHealth use?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>VeaHealth uses premium xenograft (bovine-derived bone particles), allograft (processed human donor bone), or synthetic bone substitutes — all FDA/CE-approved and proven for maxillary sinus augmentation. Your surgeon selects the optimal material based on graft volume needed and healing timeline preferences.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>What are the risks of sinus lift surgery?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The primary risk is Schneiderian membrane perforation (occurs in 10–30% of cases, usually repaired immediately without consequence). Infection risk is &lt;2% with antibiotic prophylaxis. Sinusitis is rare if post-op instructions are followed (no nose-blowing for 4 weeks). Graft failure is uncommon (&lt;5%) in non-smokers with good oral hygiene.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How many trips to Istanbul are required?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Two visits: the first for sinus lift surgery (3–5 days in Istanbul), and a second visit 6–9 months later for implant placement (5–7 days). The entire graft healing phase is monitored remotely by VeaHealth with CBCT scans at 3 and 6 months — no travel required during consolidation.</p></div></details></div></div></section><section class="cta-final" id="contact" data-surface="dark"><div class="cta-final-inner"><h2>Ready to Build Bone for<br><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--teal);">Your Dental Implants?</em></h2><p>VeaHealth coordinates your complete sinus lift journey in Istanbul — 3D planning, expert oral surgeons, premium bone graft materials, and remote monitoring throughout consolidation.</p><div class="cta-trust-row"><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Free CBCT Assessment</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Premium Bone Graft Materials</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> VIP Istanbul Concierge</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> International Warranty</div></div><div class="cta-btns">
