<span class="label">Treatment Journey</span><h2 class="title">Your Inlay/Onlay <em>Procedure</em></h2><p class="desc">Standard two-visit protocol — first visit for preparation and impression, second visit one week later for permanent bonding.</p></div><div class="proc-timeline " data-anim="up"><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">1</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Visit 1 — Day 1</span><h3>Tooth Preparation &#038; Digital Impression</h3><p>Decay is removed and the cavity is prepared with precise margins. A digital 3D scan captures the exact shape and size of the prepared cavity. A temporary filling protects the tooth for one week.</p><ul><li>Local anesthesia for comfort</li><li>Decay removal &#038; cavity prep</li><li>Digital intraoral scan taken</li><li>Temporary filling placed</li><li>Lab fabrication begins (5–7 days)</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">2</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Lab Phase — Days 2–7</span><h3>CAD/CAM Fabrication</h3><p>Your inlay or onlay is digitally designed and milled from a solid block of porcelain or zirconia in VeaHealth&#8217;s partner lab. Color is precisely matched to your natural tooth shade.</p><ul><li>Digital design in CAD software</li><li>CAM milling from solid block</li><li>Shade matching &#038; glazing</li><li>Quality control inspection</li><li>Sterilization &#038; packaging</li></ul></div></div><div class="proc-step"><div class="proc-num">3</div><div class="proc-content">
<span class="proc-tag">Visit 2 — Day 7–10</span><h3>Permanent Bonding</h3><p>The temporary filling is removed. Your custom inlay/onlay is tried in to verify fit and bite. Once confirmed, it&#8217;s permanently bonded using dental adhesive. Final polishing ensures a smooth, natural feel.</p><ul><li>Temporary filling removed</li><li>Inlay/onlay fit verification</li><li>Bite adjustment if needed</li><li>Permanent adhesive bonding</li><li>Final polishing &#038; care instructions</li></ul></div></div></div></div></section><section class="cost" id="pricing" data-surface="dark"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Transparent Pricing</span><h2 class="title title-white">What You&#8217;ll Pay — <em>Guaranteed</em></h2><p class="desc desc-white">VeaHealth locks in your price before travel. All costs include preparation, lab fabrication, temporary restoration, permanent bonding, and warranty.</p></div><div class="cost-cards " data-anim="up"><div class="cost-card"><h3>UK / US</h3><div class="location">London, New York</div><div class="cost-price">£600+</div><div class="cost-note">per inlay/onlay</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>Standard porcelain inlay/onlay</li><li>Two-visit procedure</li><li>Basic warranty (1–2 years)</li></ul></div><div class="cost-card featured">
<span class="cost-tag">Best Value</span><h3>VeaHealth Istanbul</h3><div class="location">Istanbul, Turkey</div><div class="cost-price">£180</div><div class="cost-note">all-inclusive per restoration</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>Porcelain or zirconia material</li><li>Digital 3D scanning</li><li>CAD/CAM precision milling</li><li>Temporary restoration included</li><li>Permanent adhesive bonding</li><li>5-year warranty</li><li>VeaHealth coordination</li><li>Hotel support if needed</li></ul></div><div class="cost-card"><h3>Europe</h3><div class="location">Germany, Spain</div><div class="cost-price">€350+</div><div class="cost-note">per inlay/onlay</div><ul class="cost-features"><li>Standard ceramic restoration</li><li>Two-visit protocol</li><li>Standard warranty (2 years)</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="faq" id="faq"><div class="container"><div class="" data-anim="up">
<span class="label">Patient Questions</span><h2 class="title">Frequently Asked <em>Questions</em></h2></div><div class="faq-grid " data-anim="up"><details class="faq-item"><summary>What is the difference between an inlay and an onlay?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>An inlay fits within the tooth&#8217;s cusps (the raised points) and is used when the cusps are still structurally sound. An onlay extends over one or more cusps to provide additional protection and strength when the cusps are weakened. Your dentist will determine which is appropriate based on the extent of damage.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How long do inlays and onlays last?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>With proper care, porcelain and zirconia inlays/onlays last 10–15+ years on average — significantly longer than composite fillings (5–7 years). Longevity depends on oral hygiene, bite forces, and avoiding habits like grinding or chewing ice.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is the procedure painful?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>No. Both visits are performed under local anesthesia. You&#8217;ll feel pressure during preparation but no pain. Some sensitivity is normal for a few days after bonding as the tooth adjusts to the new restoration.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Porcelain or zirconia — which is better?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Porcelain offers superior aesthetics and is ideal for visible teeth (premolars, upper molars). Zirconia is stronger and better for back molars that endure heavy chewing forces. VeaHealth&#8217;s dentists will recommend the optimal material based on the tooth location and your bite.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can I eat normally after the procedure?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. After the temporary filling (first visit), stick to soft foods on the opposite side. Once the permanent inlay/onlay is bonded (second visit), you can resume normal eating within 24 hours. Avoid extremely hard foods like ice or hard candy to prevent chipping.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How many days in Istanbul are required?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Standard protocol requires 7–10 days total. First appointment for preparation and scan, then a 5–7 day wait while the lab fabricates your restoration, then the second appointment for permanent bonding. VeaHealth can arrange hotel accommodations and sightseeing tours during the wait.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is the warranty valid internationally?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Yes. VeaHealth&#8217;s 5-year warranty on inlays and onlays is valid worldwide. If a restoration fails due to defect or bonding failure, VeaHealth coordinates repair or replacement — either remotely via a partner clinic in your country or with a return visit to Istanbul.</p></div></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Why is it so much cheaper in Istanbul?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Lower operating costs (lab fees, rent, staff salaries) in Turkey allow VeaHealth to offer the same premium materials and techniques at 60–70% less than UK/US prices. The quality is identical — same porcelain and zirconia brands, same CAD/CAM technology, same clinical standards.</p></div></details></div></div></section><section class="cta-final" id="contact" data-surface="dark"><div class="cta-final-inner"><h2>Ready for Precision<br>Porcelain Restoration?</h2><p>VeaHealth coordinates your complete inlay/onlay journey in Istanbul — digital scanning, lab-crafted precision, permanent bonding, and full support from consultation to final result.</p><div class="cta-trust-row"><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Free Online Assessment</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> Porcelain or Zirconia Materials</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> VIP Istanbul Concierge</div><div class="cta-trust-item"><div class="cta-check">✓</div> 5-Year Warranty</div></div>
